the data will help as  she makes the case  for more funding and targeted solutions  this research is very helpful to us  in terms of understanding not only the  scope or the magnitude of the challenge  but also what are the kinds of things  that would be effective because these  are treatable and they are preventable  nadia stewart global news vancouver  still ahead the fight for a fig tree  will explain  [Music]  you're watching global national  typhoon vamco has made landfall in  vietnam  although the storm is weakening there is  still a threat of flooding and  landslides  the government has evacuation plans in  place for roughly 468 thousand people  the typhoon has already done damage to  the philippines at least 67 people have  died there and the death toll is  expected to rise  as rescue crews continue their search  for dozens of people missing  the system packed winds that reached  kilometers an hour  torrential rain has triggered widespread  flooding  peru's interim president has resigned  six days after being sworn in  the country's political parties demanded  manuel mourinho step  down over the protests that have gripped  that country  thousands in peru have been staging some  of the country's largest demonstrations  in decades  but they've been marred by clashes with  police and two protesters were killed at  the hands of officers  a week ago the previous president martin  vizcarra  quit over allegations of bribery which  he denies  environmentalists in kenya are  celebrating tonight after saving  a century-old fig tree it lives in the  heart of the country's capital and was  scheduled to be removed to make way for  a highway  fig trees are important in kenya and  locals believe this particular tree  has sacred powers crystal gomencing  reports  it's a green victory this leafy towering  beacon in a busy commercial area in  nairobi  is staying put this particular fig tree  is just a symbol of the bigger picture  of what we're asking for  we want a green and clean city a green  and clean kenya  that is also climate resilient and this  means that we cannot afford to sacrifice  our green spaces for anything  including development the nearly 100  year old fig tree was slated to be  removed to make way for a new  multi-million dollar infrastructure  project  a four-lane highway built by china many  other trees were ripped from the ground  to make way for the expressway  but the fight for this one united the  community  [Music]  marches were organized and participants  loudly voiced their opposition to  uprooting the beloved tree more vocal  opposition was launched by local tribal  elders  who cited the tree's cultural and  spiritual history  this tree why we used to keep it  it used to be there because we went for  prayers there  there was a suggestion that the  four-story tall tree could be relocated  but many said that that plan was  questionable  because the tree might not be able to  survive  activists also launched a legal  challenge against the kenyan  environmental regulator for approving  the entire construction project  citing concerns over pollution and a  lack of green space in the sprawling  city  despite the challenge being before the  courts construction continued  but now after a year-long campaign  advocates got the news they had been  working for  on behalf of his excellency the  president  nms will issue a declaration  of conservation for this tree  for this iconic tree this decision today  gives me hope that activism works when  it comes to  protecting our environment and our green  spaces not only will the tree be  preserved for future generations it'll  stand as a national symbol of  environmental conservation  one that will spur on advocates as they  work to preserve  as much as the natural environment as  possible  crystal gamansen global news london  up next brittle star offers his two  cents on the covet conspiracy theories  a belgian bred racing pigeon set a world  record  as the most expensive ev